---
import AppLayout from '../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/app.css';
import '../styles/page.css';
---

<AppLayout
	title="About — doodlebooth.lol"
	description="What doodlebooth.lol is: a shared wall where anyone can draw a quick doodle and drop it in for everyone to see."
>
	<Navbar />

	<main class="page">
		<div class="page-hero">
			<div class="eyebrow">About</div>
			<h1>A shared wall for <span class="grad">tiny doodles</span></h1>
			<p class="lede">
				doodlebooth.lol is a public drawing wall. Sketch something in the booth, drop it in, and
				it lands on the wall next to everyone else's. No skill required — the messier the better.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="prose">
			<h2>The idea</h2>
			<p>
				Everyone doodles. On napkins, in the margins of notebooks, on the back of receipts — and
				then throws them away. So we built the dumbest, most honest home for them:
				<strong>one wall, open to anyone, where a 20-second scribble sits right next to
				everyone else's</strong>. No accounts, no feed algorithm, no likes to chase.
			</p>
			<p>
				A stick figure counts. A masterpiece counts. They land on the same wall and that's the
				whole point.
			</p>

			<h2>How it works</h2>
			<ol class="steps">
				<li><b>Open the booth.</b> A blank canvas, a few brushes, and some colors. No sign up, no login, no email.</li>
				<li><b>Draw something.</b> Anything. Takes twenty seconds or twenty minutes — your call.</li>
				<li><b>Drop it on the wall.</b> Your doodle joins the shared wall for everyone to see.</li>
				<li><b>Browse the rest.</b> Scroll the wall and enjoy what strangers have scribbled.</li>
			</ol>

			<h2>Real drawings, stored simply</h2>
			<p>
				Doodles are saved as images the moment you drop them in, then served from our own storage
				so the wall loads fast. Nothing is generated or mocked — every square on the wall is
				something a real person drew in the booth.
			</p>

			<div class="facts">
				<div class="fact">
					<div class="k">Who can draw</div>
					<div class="v">Anyone</div>
				</div>
				<div class="fact">
					<div class="k">Login required</div>
					<div class="v">None</div>
				</div>
				<div class="fact">
					<div class="k">Cost</div>
					<div class="v">Free</div>
				</div>
				<div class="fact">
					<div class="k">Skill needed</div>
					<div class="v">Zero</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<h2>What this isn't</h2>
			<p>
				There's no scoring, no ranking, and no reward for drawing — you're adding a doodle to a
				novelty wall and nothing more. We don't ask for your password, we don't build a profile
				of you, and we only ever store the drawing you chose to submit.
			</p>

			<div class="callout">
				<p>
					<strong>On moderation:</strong> if a doodle on the wall shouldn't be there, we'll take
					it down. No form, no questions. See the terms for what's allowed.
				</p>
			</div>

			<h2>Who made this</h2>
			<p>
				doodlebooth.lol is a small side project — built fast, deployed on Cloudflare's edge, and
				intentionally kept to one screen. It's the kind of thing that exists because it was fun
				enough to ship.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="page-cta">
			<a href="/">Go draw something →</a>
		</div>
	</main>

	<Footer />

	<script>
		import { initThemeToggle } from '../lib/theme';
		const themeToggle = document.getElementById('themeToggle');
		if (themeToggle) initThemeToggle(themeToggle);
	</script>
</AppLayout>
